+A consumer whose CPU view is deferred can provide both sources with
+`HostMemory::with_gather_and_dma_buf(pointer, gather, dma_buf)`. The gather route is tried only
+where the device imports host pointers. Before a dma-buf fallback, the gather source is asked
+for the whole import window, with `granule == length`, and must answer `GatherAnswer::Pointer`
+after mapping those pages persistently. A pieces answer or an error stops the import without
+calling the dma-buf source. The fallback exports those same pages and follows the existing
+dma-buf contracts and limits. Linux and Android also check that the materialized window is
+writable; a read-only view needs the consumer's separate writable-twin policy, not changed
+protection on the original mapping. Device loss and invalid gather-source contracts remain
+errors. The existing gather path may first retry a failed sparse import by pointer. This
+permits a deferred-view consumer to use a dma-buf-only device while materializing
+the CPU views that its imports need; it does not remove the consumer's CPU mapping budget.
+
